2026-09-27T09:57:22.7086225Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7086510Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7086981Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7087490Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7087636Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7087940Z ================
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7088119Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7088348Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7089139Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7089478Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7089644Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7090064Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7090330Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7090535Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7091133Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7091654Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7092658Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7093569Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7093757Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7094445Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7180858Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7181317Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7181807Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7182483Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7182642Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7182970Z ========
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7183127Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7185171Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7187291Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7187625Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7188333Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7189685Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7190593Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7191450Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7192107Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7192708Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7192863Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7193216Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7193436Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7195104Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7196951Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7197995Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7199529Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:57:22.7199853Z 
